[00:03.02] Lonesome Suzie never got the breaks
[00:11.70] She's always losing and so she sits and cries and shakes
[00:24.44] It's hard just to watch her and if I touch her
[00:33.38] Oh, poor Suzie, I'm wondering what to do
[00:44.28] She just sits there hoping for a friend
[00:55.74] I don't fit here but I may have a friend to lend
[01:06.32] Maybe I mistook her but I can't overlook her
[01:17.38] Must be someone who can pull her through
[01:26.58] Anyone who's felt that bad could tell me what to say
[01:37.44] Even if she just get mad, she might be better off that way
[01:50.18] And where is all the understanding?
[01:55.24] Her problems can't be that demanding
[02:00.98] Why is it she looks my way every time she starts to cry?
[02:11.28] Lonesome Suzie, I can't watch you cry no longer
[02:21.42] If you can use me until you feel a little stronger
[02:32.58] I guess just watching you has made me lonesome too
[02:42.56] Why don't we get together, what else can we do?
